@prefix cme: <http://example.org/cme#> .
@prefix chx: <http://example.org/sen0414/ch23#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/sen0414/ch23/diagrams> a owl:Ontology ; rdfs:label "SEN0414 ch23 narrative diagrams - ABox"@en ; owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch23_diagrams_abox_v1_0_0" ;
    rdfs:comment "The chapter's authored diagrams as cme:NarrativeDiagram individuals: generated by sen0414_page_data_v2_6_0.py from sen0414_ch23_diagrams_v1_0_0.py, typed by the CME narrative-to-diagram mapping (a module of cme_standards_adoption_v1_3_0.ttl, CME 0.16.0)."@en ; owl:imports <http://example.org/cme/narrative-diagram> .

chx:Diagram_ACallWithTheFailSafeOn a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "What happens when a script calls a PyAutoGUI function with the fail-safe on"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Workflow ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:ActivityDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 23, Pauses and Fail-Safes: after a function call PyAutoGUI waits one tenth of a second, and if the cursor is in a corner it raises the exception that stops the program" ; cme:elementCount 7 ;
    cme:accompanies "PauseDefault" ; cme:accompanies "FailsafeCorners" ; cme:accompanies "FailsafeFires" ; cme:accompanies "FailsafeSlam" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is a sequence of steps with one test on whether the cursor is in a corner that sends the program on or stops it: a workflow"@en .
chx:Diagram_FindingAndClickingAButton a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Finding a button in a screenshot and clicking it"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Workflow ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:ActivityDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 23, Image Recognition: locateOnScreen() looks for the picture of a button in a screenshot and returns its box, or raises ImageNotFoundException when the image cannot be found" ; cme:elementCount 7 ;
    cme:accompanies "ScreenshotImage" ; cme:accompanies "LocateBox" ; cme:accompanies "LocateAllAndClick" ; cme:accompanies "ImageNotFound" ; cme:accompanies "LocateWaits" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is a sequence of steps with a test on whether the image was found that leads to a click or to an exception: a workflow"@en .
chx:Diagram_TypingIntoTheRightWindow a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Typing a string into a window that has the focus"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Workflow ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:ActivityDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 23, Sending Keystrokes: click to make the window active, call write() to type the string and hotkey() to press a shortcut, because the focused window receives the typing" ; cme:elementCount 5 ;
    cme:accompanies "FocusDecides" ; cme:accompanies "WriteString" ; cme:accompanies "HotkeyOrder" ; cme:accompanies "SleepAndCountdown" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is a sequence of steps in which each step depends on the window the one before it made active: a workflow"@en .
chx:Diagram_ScriptToXServer a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "A script sending a click to a window through XTEST"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Interaction ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:SequenceDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 23 and the X.Org protocol documents: PyAutoGUI asks the X server to simulate the button events with XTestFakeInput and the window receives them" ; cme:elementCount 9 ;
    cme:accompanies "XTestEvents" ; cme:accompanies "SyntheticVersusReal" ; cme:accompanies "ClickSequence" ; cme:accompanies "XtermIgnoresSent" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is an exchange between the script, the library and the X server in an order that matters - the request goes out before the window gets the event: an interaction"@en .
chx:Diagram_CopyingTextWithTheClipboard a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "A script copying the text of a window through the clipboard"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Interaction ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:SequenceDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 23: the program calls pyautogui.hotkey('ctrl', 'a'), then hotkey('ctrl', 'c') and pyperclip.paste() to retrieve the text of a window" ; cme:elementCount 8 ;
    cme:accompanies "ClipboardRoundTrip" ; cme:accompanies "HotkeyOrder" ; cme:accompanies "FocusDecides" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is an exchange between the script, the window and the clipboard in an order that matters - the text is copied before it is pasted: an interaction"@en .
chx:Diagram_TheLifeOfADrag a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "A drag from the first press of the button to its release"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:LifeCycle ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:StateDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 23, Dragging the Mouse: dragTo() and drag() move the cursor with the button held down, in the steps that the duration gives, and the button is released at the new location" ; cme:elementCount 7 ;
    cme:accompanies "DragEvents" ; cme:accompanies "DragVersusMove" ; cme:accompanies "ClickSequence" ; cme:accompanies "SpiralDrawing" ; rdfs:comment "the passage follows the pointer through the states it is in during a drag and names the call that moves it from each state to the next: a life cycle"@en .
chx:Diagram_WhatAScriptCanDoWithPyAutoGUI a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "What a script can do with PyAutoGUI"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:SetOfUses ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:UseCaseDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 23: move the mouse, click, drag and scroll, take a screenshot, find an image on the screen, type text and press hotkeys, and display message boxes" ; cme:elementCount 10 ;
    cme:accompanies "MovingTheMouse" ; cme:accompanies "Clicking" ; cme:accompanies "DraggingAndScrolling" ; cme:accompanies "Screenshots" ; cme:accompanies "ImageRecognition" ; cme:accompanies "TypingText" ; cme:accompanies "MessageBoxes" ; rdfs:comment "the chapter lists independent things a script can ask the library to do - move, click, drag, scroll, look, type, ask - a set of uses, not a sequence"@en .
chx:Diagram_ControllingTheKeyboardAndMouseAtAGlance a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Controlling the keyboard and mouse at a glance: six branches"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:TopicAndParts ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:MindMap ; cme:readFrom "chapter 23, the opening of each of its main parts: installing and sending input, staying on track, controlling the mouse, the screen and images, windows and the keyboard, and scripts and practice" ; cme:elementCount 25 ;
    cme:accompanies "InstallingAndSendingInput" ; cme:accompanies "StayingOnTrack" ; cme:accompanies "MouseControl" ; cme:accompanies "ScreenAndImages" ; cme:accompanies "WindowsAndKeyboard" ; cme:accompanies "ScriptsAndPractice" ; rdfs:comment "the chapter classifies one topic, controlling a computer with a script, by what each part is about and lists examples under each - a topic and its parts, laid out to remember, with the one idea that holds for every part stated once at the root"@en .
